description:
Add unit test asserting 169.254.0.0/16 appears as REJECT rule in per-VM filter chain (not just any CIDR in permanent_deny_cidrs()). Pins IMDS specifically.

Files:
- crates/m80-net-outbound/tests/network-outbound-nat/iptables.rs

Test:
```rust
#[test]
fn imds_cidr_rejected_in_filter_chain() {
    let state = ready_state();
    let chain = outbound_nat_filter_chain(&state);
    let comment = outbound_nat_rule_comment(&state);
    let mut ops = RecordingPolicyOps::default();
    apply_outbound_nat_policy_with_ops(&mut ops, &state).unwrap();
    assert!(
        ops.chain_rules("filter", &chain).contains(&vec![
            "-d", "169.254.0.0/16",
            "-m", "comment", "--comment", &comment,
            "-j", "REJECT"
        ]),
        "169.254.0.0/16 REJECT rule missing from per-VM filter chain"
    );
}
```

No new iptables rules — already installed. Test pins the rule exists.

Acceptance:
- test passes (existing rule)
- removing 169.254.0.0/16 from permanent_deny_cidrs() makes test fail (verified locally before commit)
- CHANGELOG (Security): pin IMDS link-local block as regression test

Add unit test asserting 169.254.0.0/16 REJECT rule precedes the terminal ACCEPT in chain order. Without ordering check, a REJECT rule appended after ACCEPT would be unreachable but still pass a "rule exists" assertion.

Files:
- crates/m80-net-outbound/tests/network-outbound-nat/iptables.rs

Test:
```rust
#[test]
fn imds_reject_precedes_terminal_accept_in_filter_chain() {
    let state = ready_state();
    let chain = outbound_nat_filter_chain(&state);
    let mut ops = RecordingPolicyOps::default();
    apply_outbound_nat_policy_with_ops(&mut ops, &state).unwrap();
    let rules = ops.chain_rules("filter", &chain);
    let imds_pos = rules.iter().position(|r| r.contains(&"169.254.0.0/16"))
        .expect("169.254.0.0/16 REJECT rule not found");
    let accept_pos = rules.iter().rposition(|r| r.last() == Some(&"ACCEPT"))
        .expect("terminal ACCEPT rule not found");
    assert!(imds_pos < accept_pos, "IMDS REJECT at {imds_pos} must precede terminal ACCEPT at {accept_pos}");
}
```

Acceptance:
- test passes against current order
- reordering rules so REJECT trails ACCEPT makes test fail (verified locally)
- CHANGELOG (Security)

